From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 08:38:55 +0200
Subject: MIPS: mips-gic: add the VP-local watchdog registers

The GIC provides every Virtual Processor with a watchdog timer, but the
header only exposes GIC_Vx_WD_MAP -- the register that routes the
expiry interrupt. The three registers that make up the timer itself,
GIC_Vx_WD_CONFIG0 (0x090), GIC_Vx_WD_COUNT0 (0x094) and
GIC_Vx_WD_INITIAL0 (0x098), have no accessors, so a driver cannot arm,
feed or read the thing it maps. The offsets are the ones the
pre-rewrite MIPS GIC header carried before commit 1fad12cd5ef4
("irqchip: mips-gic: Remove linux/irqchip/mips-gic.h").

Add them along with the GIC_Vx_WD_CONFIG0 field definitions. The TYPE
field selects what an expiry does:

  0  interrupt only -- the countdown stops at zero and stays there,
  1  SCD (Second CountDown) -- the first expiry sets WDINTR and reloads,
     a second expiry while WDINTR is still set requests a reset,
  2  PIT -- reload and interrupt forever, no reset.

So SCD is the only setting under which the block behaves as a watchdog.
WDINTR and WDRESET are the corresponding status bits, cleared by
writing them back.

The field positions are not documented in any header this architecture
has ever carried; they were established by exercising the timer on a
MIPS interAptiv part, one field at a time, against the observable
behaviour above.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/mips-gic.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/mips-gic.h
index fd9da5e3beaa..74cb2ef35d8a 100644
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/mips-gic.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/mips-gic.h
@@ -285,6 +285,23 @@ GIC_VX_ACCESSOR_RW(32, 0x080, other)
 GIC_VX_ACCESSOR_RO(32, 0x088, ident)
 #define GIC_VX_IDENT_VPNUM		GENMASK(5, 0)
 
+/* GIC_Vx_WD_CONFIG0 - Configure the local Virtual Processor's watchdog */
+GIC_VX_ACCESSOR_RW(32, 0x090, wd_config0)
+#define GIC_VX_WD_CONFIG0_WDRESET	BIT(7)
+#define GIC_VX_WD_CONFIG0_WDINTR	BIT(6)
+#define GIC_VX_WD_CONFIG0_NWAIT		BIT(5)
+#define GIC_VX_WD_CONFIG0_DEBUG		BIT(4)
+#define GIC_VX_WD_CONFIG0_TYPE		GENMASK(2, 1)
+#define GIC_VX_WD_CONFIG0_TYPE_SCD	0x1
+#define GIC_VX_WD_CONFIG0_TYPE_PIT	0x2
+#define GIC_VX_WD_CONFIG0_START		BIT(0)
+
+/* GIC_Vx_WD_COUNT0 - Current value of the local watchdog's countdown */
+GIC_VX_ACCESSOR_RW(32, 0x094, wd_count0)
+
+/* GIC_Vx_WD_INITIAL0 - Value the local watchdog's countdown reloads from */
+GIC_VX_ACCESSOR_RW(32, 0x098, wd_initial0)
+
 /* GIC_Vx_COMPARE - Value to compare with GIC_SH_COUNTER */
 GIC_VX_ACCESSOR_RW(64, 0x0a0, compare)
 
